      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "**Read both status panels before using this report.** Tables use the latest observed snapshot per cluster and CronJob UID, including null values, then apply strict >90-day filters relative to the dashboard end time. The query pre-filters to CronJobs created more than 90 days before now (creation time never changes), which keeps the record count low.\n\n**Setup:** Grafana 11.6+ with transformation variable interpolation (`${__to}`); datasource time field `@timestamp`; source fields must match the supplied names. Dates must be ISO-8601 or epoch milliseconds. The cluster variable needs an aggregatable field (use `.keyword` if your mapping requires it).\n\n**Coverage:** Raw queries return at most 10,000 newest snapshots. A red record count means incomplete coverage: narrow the time window, keeping at least one fresh snapshot per job. Records missing a UID are excluded.\n\n**Panel 1:** latest snapshot has a last scheduled time older than 90 days. **Panel 2:** latest snapshot has no last scheduled time. Missing does not prove never scheduled, so check Last Seen and the raw record.\n\n**Interpretation:** Suspended jobs are included. Recently deleted jobs remain until their records leave the window; Last Seen is the latest snapshot, not proof the job exists. Snapshots must hold complete resource state, not partial update events. Conflicting snapshots with identical timestamps cannot be ordered reliably."
